  "description": "DAPDUV crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C104 H214 Co6 Er8 O62 P6. From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 10 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Co1 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3 (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 10 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er4A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Co1A (Co) has 6 O neighbors; Co2A (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co3A (Co) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 22 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.155-3.999 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.82-119.68°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [CoII6ErIII8(μ3-OH)8(O3P tBu)6(O2C tBu)16(H2O)2(MeCN)2](MeCN) (x = 2, y = 1). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
